{
  "info": {
    "_postman_id": "carex-rest-api-v1",
    "name": "CareX \u2014 End-to-End Healthcare REST API",
    "description": "Versioned CareX REST API training collection. Uses synthetic tenant data. Run in order: public discovery, patient signup/login, availability, appointment lifecycle, then staff lifecycle. Appointment booking is confirmed immediately in the current CareX business model; there is no separate doctor-approval state.\n\nFresh-run workflow: patient and staff preflights follow their own login. All generated IDs are saved to the active environment and collection. Use the isolated synthetic Dev environment. Default login uses seeded demo accounts. Enable runSignup only with a fresh patientEmail. MFA verification runs only when login returns a challenge; supply mfaCode from the captured/test mailbox. Enable runAccountRecovery only for a disposable identity, supplying resetToken and newPassword. Logout follows all protected operations. Never export current bearer tokens or use this write-enabled workflow on production.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
